1","accession":"Q12882","score":8.3687},{"name":null,"compound_id":"Z1437025116_1_T1","accession":"Q12882","score":8.35796},{"name":null,"compound_id":"Z1087975826_1_T1","accession":"Q12882","score":8.35529}],"notes":[]}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000188641","entrez_id":["1806"],"uniprot":["Q12882"],"ncbi_summary":"The protein encoded by this gene is a pyrimidine catabolic enzyme and the initial and rate-limiting factor in the pathway of uracil and thymidine catabolism. Mutations in this gene result in dihydropyrimidine dehydrogenase deficiency, an error in pyrimidine metabolism associated with thymine-uraciluria and an increased risk of toxicity in cancer patients receiving 5-fluorouracil chemotherapy. Two transcript variants encoding different isoforms have been found for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, May 2009].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q12882","text":"Catalyzes the reduction of uracil and thymine in the initial step of reductive pyrimidine catabolism, a pathway that yields beta-alanine from uracil and beta-aminoisobutyrate from thymine (PubMed:1512248). Also capable of degrading the chemotherapeutic drug 5-fluorouracil (PubMed:1512248)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":["Q12882"]}